1
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:30,760
Thursday before everything starts: "Hello! You have come in via late registration for the program in Örebro.

2
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:35,440
- How fun!
- Well, and when do I start?
"On Monday."
So that...

3
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:37,500
- * Laughter * - so ...

4
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:40,140
I was very annoying, I know.

5
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:44,900
I would jump on the medical program and book my life for 5½ years, as well.

6
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:49,000
So it was a bit like this: "But God, what have I given up on?"

7
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:51,140
And how will this be?

8
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:56,240
At the same time, it was very cool too, because for the first time you would jump on an education -

9
00:01:56,260 --> 00:02:00,440
- That would lead to what you wanted to be the rest of your life.

10
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:15,060
"I'll google, wait a bit!"

11
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:17,960
I have zero sense of geography, so I'm starting to google.

12
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:21,300
- "Yes, but it's easy to get there!"
- "Yeah. Where are you going to live?"

13
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,760
Yes, that's the next good question too ...

14
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:28,340
I took a sabbatical to be able to digest everything and recover from high school.

15
00:02:28,340 --> 00:02:32,280
- It's pretty ... especially if you go in for grades - yes, of course.

16
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:36,920
I didn't invest so much on the college exam.
You can get in through that too.

17
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,060
And then it became that you ...

18
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:43,640
I didn't feel ready to get into the studies again.
- No, I understand.

19
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:19,720
I knew I was going to study, because I just come from high school.

20
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:23,360
- Yes exactly.
- I took the student this summer, and I already knew -

21
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:27,640
- That I wanted to continue because I want to be finished earlier, later.

22
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:33,060
I had been here the year before and checked in, because I saw Örebro as a suitable candidate.

23
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:37,680
It was close, but I still wanted to test my wings and move to a new city.

24
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:41,560
- But still not too far from the parents.
- No, of course.

25
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:47,080
It was the first time.
I had lived at home for 19 years before moving here.

26
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:53,420
So it was a big step to start living yourself.
Have your own accommodation, wash, cook.

27
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:58,640
I remember how I stood at home and practiced frying mom Scan's meatballs to be ready.

28
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:34,100
I still haven't gone up in rank from sausage stroganoff.
I'm still there.

29
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:37,820
- I understand.
- the best I know is when you don't have to cook -

30
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:41,220
- And you can eat roasted sandwiches for dinner.
- Yes, but I also know it.

31
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:45,680
My favorite food is just sandwiches.

32
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:50,220
It's so simple, it's just buying bread, butter and optional toppings

33
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:53,100
- It's kind of better than anything.
- I know!

34
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:55,760
Prio one is to pass the studies.

35
00:08:55,760 --> 00:09:00,180
After all, that is the reason why you are in the city and plug in at Örebro University.

36
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:03,100
- It's for the sake of studies.
- Yes.

37
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:14,860
And so I feel that, shit, I don't have my phone on me.

38
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:19,340
- Okay, my bank card ... I'll shop afterwards.
- You should live.

39
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:21,460
I want to be able to come home.

40
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:24,620
Shit, I put it in the toilet.

41
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:29,160
- So I just get up.
I sat in the middle of an auditorium.
- You just stand up?

42
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:34,260
Yes, in panic I get up very fast.
Everyone looks at me and wonders what's going on.

43
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:38,240
The lecturer also looks at me and wonders what is happening.
Does anyone have died, kind of?

44
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:42,820
I'm just running out.
"Excuse me, excuse, let go of me!"

45
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:47,080
Goes from the middle towards the edge and out of the hall.
